From 25913193ec1a5bff2db3960ef20c9b38ce3d4929 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Giuseppe Maggio <jertlok@proton.me>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 17:45:17 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 65/68] ipa: softisp: Add contrast autofocus

A hill climb over the sharpness statistic, normalised by mean luminance:
a coarse scan over the lens range, a fine step either side of the best
position, then lock, with a rescan in continuous mode when sharpness
drops for several frames.

It implements the AfMode (manual, auto, continuous), AfTrigger and
LensPosition controls and reports AfState. LensPosition is in dioptres
and converted to actuator codes with a piecewise linear map from the
tuning file, so the algorithm needs no knowledge of the lens driver's
code range.

Assisted-by: Claude
Signed-off-by: Giuseppe Maggio <jertlok@proton.me>
---
